    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d359">

                <pb facs="0328" n="318" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg318"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/4–2949</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Director of the China Program of the Economic
                        Cooperation Administration</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cleveland</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Director of the Office of Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Butterworth</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-29">29 April 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Walt</hi>: I am sending you a particularly
                    interesting letter, classified “Top Secret”, from Allen Griffin. This letter was
                    apparently written shortly before Mr. Lapham returned to China. It recommends
                    strongly that no action be taken to set up a Taiwan operation under <pb
                        facs="0329" n="319" xml:id="pg319"/> present circumstances, and giving the
                    present elements with whom it would be necessary to deal there.</p>
                <p>I would be interested to know if you are getting similar advice from Livie
                    Merchant.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harlan Cleveland</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d359-a1.xml" xpointer="d359-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
